WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.137
Before analyzing a new dataset, inspect it.

00:00:03.137 --> 00:00:08.487
In this example, we use several simple tools that should become automatic habits.

00:00:08.487 --> 00:00:10.807
Head shows the first few rows.

00:00:10.807 --> 00:00:17.392
This helps us understand the general structure and whether the values look reasonable.

00:00:17.392 --> 00:00:20.317
Shape gives us two numbers: the number of rows and the number of columns.

00:00:20.317 --> 00:00:22.842
Columns gives us the column names.

00:00:22.842 --> 00:00:26.357
Sample returns a few randomly selected rows.

00:00:26.357 --> 00:00:31.227
Here we set random_state so the same sample appears each time.

00:00:31.227 --> 00:00:34.637
Click Run and look at each output separately.

00:00:34.637 --> 00:00:39.552
Imagine receiving a file that someone tells you contains ten thousand records.

00:00:39.552 --> 00:00:45.557
If shape shows only nine hundred rows, that is something we should investigate immediately.

00:00:45.557 --> 00:00:48.452
The same idea applies after cleaning.

00:00:48.452 --> 00:00:52.032
If we start with one thousand rows and end with six hundred,

00:00:52.032 --> 00:00:55.602
we need to understand why four hundred rows disappeared.

00:00:55.602 --> 00:01:00.042
A simple row count can detect serious analytical problems.

00:01:00.042 --> 00:01:03.982
So one of the most important habits in this module is this:

00:01:03.982 --> 00:01:10.292
know the size and basic structure of your data before and after major transformations.
